ally he  hardly looks to have aged at all say for  a few wrinkles here and there with a  nice comedic touch zorro at age 40  declares that he has mastered the four  sword style and at age 60 he's even  upgraded to five swords now i'm not even  sure i wanna know how he's holding that  fourth and fifth sword but feel free to  let me know if you have any guesses this  goes to show though that zaro's pursuit  of strength doesn't have to end just  because he's the strongest swordsman in  the world even if he overcomes mihawk  and stands above any other challenger  there's still one important opponent  that he'll have left himself i mean zaro  can always continue lifting his  oversized weights and surpassing his own  limits he'll likely maintain his  disciplined training rather than resting  on his laurels after all he's already  achieved so much in the story and that  hasn't changed his razor sharp focus on  improving himself at all so far now as  we've mentioned earlier he has already  learned to cut steel but that's only  really the beginning of what zorro has  accomplished he has helped a lot to hold  his crew together in the toughest  moments such as when usopp left the  straw hat crew during water 7. he's  defeated countless formidable foes like  the legendary warrior from wano ryuma  gaming the fabled sword shoes wii and  also in thriller bark who could forget  him taking on all of luffy's pain in  order to save the rest of the crew and  in a truly iconic moment professing that  nothing happens and recently in wano  like we mentioned he's managed not only  to scar kaido a feat formerly only  accomplished by odin but also to  temporarily block a dual attack from  kaido and big mom he also of course  tamed odin's sword enma and evidently  even fought back the grim reaper himself  and as we enter the final saga zorro  shows no signs of slowing down in the  slightest just like mihawk he may live a  quiet and reserved life though with  barrels of sake i guess instead of